    "problemDescription": "# House of ekko — Cross-Bin Heap Corruption to FSOP (glibc 2.43)\n\n**Securinets CTF 2026 · Pwn · Solved**\n\n> **Challenge:** `House of ekko`  \n> **Description:** *a \"new house\" in da house*  \n> **Service:** `pwn2.securinets.tn:7001`  \n> **Flag:** `Securinets{lets_hope_i_dont_push_the_revenge}`\n\n## TL;DR\n\nThe challenge is a two-slot heap note manager running with a bundled **glibc 2.43**. `delete()` calls `free()` but never clears the pointer; `show()` and subsequent frees can therefore access an already-freed chunk. We first leak a `main_arena` pointer, then repeatedly reclaim and re-forge a chunk embedded inside a larger allocation. By manipulating the allocator's **smallbin and largebin linked-list metadata**, we make `malloc()` return a pointer into libc's `main_arena` rather than the heap.\n\nThe final write overlaps **`_IO_list_all`**, allowing us to install a forged `FILE` structure. Its legitimate `_IO_wfile_jumps` table and attacker-controlled wide-data jump table ultimately redirect an exit-time stdio flush to `system(\"  sh;\")`. The resulting shell provides the flag.\n\n**The interesting part:** a classical largebin write was rejected by modern `nextsize` integrity checks. The working attack instead abuses stale references across **different bin sizes**, then carefully preserves libc locale state so the final menu input still works.\n\n## 1. Exploit at a glance\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"Two-slot heap note manager\"] --> B[\"Dangling pointer after free\"]\n    B --> C[\"Show freed chunk → unsorted-bin leak\"]\n    C --> D[\"Compute libc base / main_arena\"]\n    D --> E[\"Forge B chunk inside large C allocation\"]\n    E --> F[\"Reclassify stale B between smallbin and largebin\"]\n    F --> G[\"Poison smallbin fd/bk using libc largebin head\"]\n    G --> H[\"malloc returns libc + 0x1d23f8\"]\n    H --> I[\"Write fake FILE / wide_data and _IO_list_all\"]\n    I --> J[\"Exit → glibc stdio flush → system\"]\n    J --> K[\"Shell → flag\"]\n    classDef success fill:#174e37,color:#fff,stroke:#174e37\n    class K success\n```",
